                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Seems to be an abandoned title. Laterst discussion topic is from 2016.\n\nThere doesn't seem to be any story to speak of. You spawn in a level, and shoot at zombies spawning at you.\n\nthe controls are clunky, confusing, overly complex and unresponsive, and I spent most of the time playing this trying to figure out how to get rid of the huge square-shaped grenade menus above my hands because of the tracpad movement being my preferred mode of locomotion and the trackpad left button brings it up if you press it by accident. Drawing and holstering weapons is awkward.\n\nEnemies seem to be able to move inside the player hitbox, at which point you are pretty much screwed as you can't shoot the zombies or hit something inside you with melee.\n\nThe weapons and the sound effects feel weak. That's about all the sound effects I heard so far, the zombies have learned to shuffle without making any kind of sound. The models are pretty low quality (blue-faced zombies?) and the levels, if you can call them that, are uninspired and lack any detail, much like the zombies themselves. Graphically it reminds me of Second Life in 2006.\n\nI got this game as part of a Bundle, and I still feel ripped off. Save your money, and buy something else.",
